{"id":"01a0657e-01ae-792a-90d2-e3f0491e8cd0","chapterSlug":"rw6-50 I","paragraph":466,"wording":"[Autumn Knight]","event":"named","holderQuote":"Another book. This one—Necromancy, Its Rise and Fall, by Sir Hilten, [Autumn Knight] of the Order of Seasons. She hadn’t read it. Ilvriss went on."}
{"id":"01a0657e-01ae-719e-910b-ffc5dab76fde","chapterSlug":"rw6-42 E","paragraph":448,"wording":"[Autumn Knight]","event":"named","holderQuote":"Sir Kelm was a Knight of the Autumn, or a Fall Knight. Or an [Autumn Knight] if you wanted to be precise, but ‘Fall Knight’ was a joke the younger members of the Order sometimes used to refer to the lower level of skill in combat the Knights of the Autumn possessed. They were scholars or [Knights] who pursued projects or simply took to magic more than most [Knights]."}
